190
00:15:21,978 --> 00:15:27,940
First drag only the assembly slider and watch the lock point move.

191
00:15:27,960 --> 00:15:32,382
Note the two settings where it leaves 0.4 to 0.6,

192
00:15:32,402 --> 00:15:35,192
and compare them with the book.

193
00:15:35,592 --> 00:15:38,816
Task one. Press Scramble tension,

194
00:15:38,836 --> 00:15:43,732
which imitates a machine someone has fiddled with.

195
00:15:44,132 --> 00:15:49,907
First see which way the lock point has gone and whether the cloth puckers.

196
00:15:49,927 --> 00:15:54,763
Decide whether one thread is relatively too tight or both are,

197
00:15:54,783 --> 00:15:56,408
and only then adjust.

198
00:15:56,808 --> 00:16:02,254
Task two. Press Machine with a loose bobbin, and bobbin dots show on top.

199
00:16:02,274 --> 00:16:07,346
This time you may move only the bobbin slider, leaving the assembly,

200
00:16:07,366 --> 00:16:09,668
the thread and the cloth alone.

201
00:16:10,068 --> 00:16:15,568
Task three. Switch to four plies of denim at 5000 rpm or more.

202
00:16:15,588 --> 00:16:21,712
First look for a usable region with Tex 24 and see how big the purple

203
00:16:21,732 --> 00:16:23,225
breakage area is,

204
00:16:23,625 --> 00:16:31,337
then change to heavier Tex 40 thread and get a stitch that is balanced,

205
00:16:31,357 --> 00:16:33,297
firm and unbroken.

206
00:16:33,697 --> 00:16:36,155
Task four. Two plies of lining.

207
00:16:36,175 --> 00:16:42,551
Keep it balanced and lower both threads together until they're just firm enough,

208
00:16:42,571 --> 00:16:45,590
with pucker no more than 0.15 percent.

